Right now Pantheon often treats an operator as either present or absent. It would be stronger to give every operator a track-record weight.

engineering ormus is almost a perfect worked example of this doctrine. It rejects unsupported ORMUS chemistry but extracts the computational anatomy—ionic inventory → selective separation → material recovery → water reuse—and rebuilds it from ordinary chemical-engineering mechanisms. 

That is Semantic Router + Indigo Hammer + Reality Stitch in one sequence:

\text{questionable ontology}
\overset{Vivisection}{\longrightarrow}
